==English==

===Etymology===
Supposed to represent the sound of snoring.

===Pronunciation===
* {{qualifier|as spelled}} {{IPA|/zː/|lang=en}}
* {{qualifier|imitation of snoring}} {{IPA|/f͡ŋ/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|Zzz.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# A snoring sound, implying that somebody is [[asleep]].

====Translations====
{{trans-top}}
* Russian: {{t|ru|хррр}} {{qualifier|colloquial, not used in books; understood, but used less frequently than zzz}}
{{trans-mid}}
* Vietnamese: {{t+|vi|khò khò}}, {{t|vi|khò sú}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|zzzs|zzzing|zzzed}}

# {{lb|en|onomatopoeia}} To [[sleep]] or [[snore]].
#* {{quote-book|year=1909|author=H. G. Wells|title=Tono-Bungay|url=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Page%3ATono-Bungay.djvu/469|page=461|passage=He lay back on his pillow, made a faint '''zzzing''' sound that ceased, and presently and quite quietly he died &mdash; greatly comforted by my assurance.}}
#* {{quote-book|year=1996|author=Charlotte Abrams|title=The Silents|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=H8I6MWc5MogC&pg=PA42&dq=zzzed&hl=en&sa=X&ei=YLcVUavPFKjfigL0lYCwBg&ved=0CDwQ6AEwAQ|page=42|passage=He '''zzzed''' for a long time, bobbing back and forth, and then he let us go, pointing to two empty seats across the aisle and motioning for us to sit down.}}

